From bd0cd6f43af3ba95d3259c29a01d5a0dca3e1e9b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: bluebird <linlanxi7552659@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 16 Jul 2026 21:57:29 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] DevTools: make loadUnpacked userScripts access atomic

Add optional expectedId and userScriptsAccess parameters to Extensions.loadUnpacked. Validate the final Chromium extension ID after manifest and policy checks, seed the persistent preference and current state before activation, and roll both back together with any newly installed registry entry unless installation completes enabled.

Cover keyed and path-derived IDs, omitted and explicit access states, first-worker availability, restart persistence, permission and security gates, injected rollback, and the existing live setter.

